                            <h3 id="mp-rideflow">RideFlow</h3>
                            <p class="mp-proof-sub">A full-stack rideshare platform for riders, drivers and administrators, built solo in a course designed for teams. Riders request rides, drivers accept and complete them, and admins run the platform, with fares and payment records underneath.</p>
                            <ul class="mp-facts three">
                                <li><b>3</b><span>USER ROLES</span></li>
                                <li><b>4</b><span>DATA TABLES</span></li>
                                <li><b>33</b><span>AUTOMATED TESTS</span></li>
                            </ul>
                            <ul class="mp-proof-list">
                                <li>The full ride lifecycle, from request to accept to pickup to completion, with the fare billed automatically at the end and a printable receipt</li>
                                <li>Row-level security enforced on the server: riders, drivers and admins each see and change only what their role allows</li>
                                <li>An AI feature that prompts an LLM with RideFlow’s own data, plus a context-based chatbot</li>
